WEBVTT

00:02.770 --> 00:05.240
<i>Humans are terrifying creatures.</i>

00:17.260 --> 00:19.310
<i>They take our lives,</i>

00:23.220 --> 00:24.730
<i>steal our wealth,</i>

00:27.730 --> 00:32.280
<i>and strip us of our dignity. That's 
what I was taught, from an early age.</i>

00:34.840 --> 00:38.250
<i>And it turned out to be true.</i>

00:41.670 --> 00:42.520
<i>Except...</i>

02:17.530 --> 02:24.990
#2 The Princess Begins Adventuring.

02:41.640 --> 02:43.270
So, what's next?

02:43.270 --> 02:44.890
Wild boar hunting.

02:44.890 --> 02:46.060
Where?

02:46.060 --> 02:46.900
Over there.

02:48.700 --> 02:50.310
Human territory...

02:50.310 --> 02:51.690
Human territory.

02:53.400 --> 02:58.400
Does your grandfather have us 
confused with handymen or something?

02:58.660 --> 03:00.150
I mean, we kind of are.

03:00.150 --> 03:01.510
We are indeed.

03:02.410 --> 03:05.160
The two of you are lacking 
in awareness of how you

03:05.160 --> 03:07.300
represent the proud Kingdom of Elenoir!

03:07.630 --> 03:09.040
You, Tessia, in particular—

03:09.040 --> 03:10.290
Stop!

03:17.250 --> 03:19.010
Well, we should get going.

03:25.800 --> 03:26.780
Ow!

03:31.070 --> 03:32.610
You little—

03:37.060 --> 03:38.030
Now you've done it!

03:38.370 --> 03:39.460
Wall of Water.

03:48.190 --> 03:49.660
They're everywhere, aren't they?

03:49.660 --> 03:51.460
I wish they weren't.

03:53.220 --> 03:55.480
You shouldn't waste your time on them.

03:55.910 --> 03:56.970
Come again?

03:56.970 --> 03:58.820
We can't hear you!

03:58.820 --> 04:01.340
I said you shouldn't waste 
your time on them!

04:01.870 --> 04:04.590
I make it a point to face any challengers!

04:04.590 --> 04:06.830
You're so cool, Tessia!

04:07.410 --> 04:09.100
This is asinine.

04:15.450 --> 04:18.550
Come on. We're taking 
this one, right? Let's go.

04:18.550 --> 04:20.110
Okay!

04:33.120 --> 04:36.840
Tessia, as you're aware,

04:36.840 --> 04:41.690
the relationships between
elves, humans, and dwarves

04:41.690 --> 04:44.130
are frayed from a long period of conflict.

04:57.860 --> 05:02.890
The three-kingdom treaty 
brought an end to that.

05:03.880 --> 05:07.910
But the treaty only exists 
between the three kingdoms.

05:19.620 --> 05:23.010
The hearts of their inhabitants 
are still steeped in that conflict.

05:23.540 --> 05:30.190
Until an end is brought to that feeling,
 the treaty is not truly complete.

05:37.690 --> 05:42.690
Which is why, Tessia, you 
must serve as an example.

05:54.420 --> 05:56.210
We're getting attacked a lot, aren't we?

05:56.750 --> 05:58.900
Elves fetch a high price.

05:58.900 --> 06:01.010
The chances of everyone getting 
along don't look good to me.

06:01.010 --> 06:02.460
You're right.

06:03.050 --> 06:06.720
But I'm not ready to give up yet.

06:10.180 --> 06:11.970
Okay, let's walk.

06:16.820 --> 06:19.820
Do you think we should cover up our ears?

06:19.820 --> 06:21.940
Nah. They'll see right 
through something like that.

06:21.940 --> 06:23.730
As-is, then.

06:24.170 --> 06:26.430
They'll hate us for the simple 
fact that we're elves.

06:26.430 --> 06:29.530
But we're going to help.

06:29.530 --> 06:31.740
I have a hard time believing that.

06:32.670 --> 06:34.740
We don't need help from elves!

06:35.500 --> 06:36.420
Leave!

06:38.830 --> 06:39.850
Huh...

06:54.260 --> 06:56.020
<i>Lucas Wykes.</i>

06:56.700 --> 07:00.480
<i>The Wykes are a powerful 
force in the Sapin Kingdom.</i>

07:00.480 --> 07:04.150
<i>Which makes it strange they have 
elvish blood in their family.</i>

07:07.000 --> 07:07.890
<i>I wonder why.</i>

07:09.370 --> 07:10.850
Hey, Elijah.

07:11.790 --> 07:16.280
What's a human like you got to 
do with the dwarf royal family?

07:16.280 --> 07:18.660
Or maybe you're actually a dwarf?

07:19.140 --> 07:20.910
It's complicated.

07:21.300 --> 07:24.170
I notice you seem to 
be part elf, yourself.

07:24.460 --> 07:30.680
The aim of the Wykes family 
is to produce powerful mages.

07:30.680 --> 07:31.930
And to do that—

07:32.220 --> 07:37.340
They're willing to welcome elves, who 
excel at mana control, into the family.

07:37.780 --> 07:40.430
Even if there's a conflict 
with the race at large.

07:43.480 --> 07:46.000
Eavesdropping is rude, you know.

07:46.000 --> 07:47.260
My apologies.

07:47.940 --> 07:53.090
<i>It seems like his family 
has some progressive ideas.</i>

07:53.090 --> 07:54.100
<i>Either that,</i>

07:54.100 --> 07:57.450
<i>or they're ambitious enough that they're 
willing to do whatever it takes.</i>

08:00.540 --> 08:02.680
I intend to use this power 
so that no one in Sapin...

08:03.110 --> 08:05.250
No, no one on the entire 
Dicathen continent

08:05.250 --> 08:07.270
will contest my standing 
as the greatest mage.

08:07.270 --> 08:10.210
That is my duty as a member 
of the Wykes family.

08:12.940 --> 08:15.470
Really? Good luck.

08:15.800 --> 08:21.230
Hey, what do you mean 
by "good luck," exactly?

08:22.130 --> 08:26.230
Lucas, we have differing goals.

08:26.520 --> 08:27.480
Huh?

08:28.410 --> 08:30.890
I don't need to be the strongest anymore.

08:34.220 --> 08:35.630
Do you have our next quest?

08:35.630 --> 08:38.200
Yeah. It's going to be a bit of a journey.

08:38.200 --> 08:39.240
Sounds like fun.

08:42.490 --> 08:44.750
Can we just talk?!

08:44.750 --> 08:46.290
You're in the way! Shut up!

08:48.060 --> 08:50.500
Do you know about the mana beasts 
that have been appearing around town?

08:51.700 --> 08:53.130
Not really.

08:53.130 --> 08:55.780
Do you know where we can find them?!

08:55.780 --> 08:57.390
Say that again?

09:00.220 --> 09:03.850
You tried, Tessia. You really did.

09:03.850 --> 09:05.590
I can't blame their response.

09:05.930 --> 09:08.900
We'd react the same way if 
humans came to our country.

09:09.960 --> 09:13.400
They could at least hear us out.

09:14.700 --> 09:16.910
Ow! What?

09:17.640 --> 09:18.630
I got her.

09:18.630 --> 09:20.060
You sure did.

09:21.140 --> 09:23.160
Can I help you two?!

09:23.540 --> 09:25.930
The boar has been coming from the east.

09:28.490 --> 09:30.670
Thank you for telling us.

09:31.320 --> 09:33.800
Hey, why'd you tell us?

09:34.090 --> 09:35.990
They're causing a lot of trouble.

09:35.990 --> 09:37.750
You're going to get rid of them, right?

09:37.750 --> 09:39.180
Leave it to us!

09:39.900 --> 09:41.570
The acorn hit her, though.

09:41.570 --> 09:43.430
Are elves weak?

09:43.430 --> 09:47.440
I am not weak! I just... 
had my guard down!

09:47.440 --> 09:51.820
Normally, I would gracefully have 
dodged! Am I clear on this?

09:48.470 --> 09:50.940
And this is our next plaything?

09:51.220 --> 09:54.420
Yes. I forget what her name is.

09:54.730 --> 09:57.150
She, as an individual, isn't significant.

09:57.150 --> 09:59.450
But who she is will be crucial.

09:59.950 --> 10:02.440
The princess of the Elenoir Kingdom...

10:02.750 --> 10:08.470
That should be more than enough 
to damage this ridiculous treaty.

10:08.470 --> 10:10.460
I'd say you're right.

10:10.460 --> 10:13.410
I've prepared a gift for the princess.

10:13.800 --> 10:16.470
I just hope she'll like it.

10:52.970 --> 10:53.990
Let's do this!

10:53.990 --> 10:54.410
Right!

10:54.410 --> 10:54.960
'Kay.

11:11.490 --> 11:12.600
We got it!

11:14.230 --> 11:16.860
Mana beast or not, it 
was just a wild boar.

11:16.860 --> 11:18.520
No match for us...

11:24.340 --> 11:25.020
Fey!

11:25.020 --> 11:26.370
Eyes in front!

11:33.910 --> 11:34.740
Did you see that?

11:34.740 --> 11:35.630
Yeah.

11:40.090 --> 11:42.630
Our magic isn't working on this thing.

11:49.640 --> 11:55.150
While they have prodigious talent 
with mana, elves have fragile bodies.

11:55.390 --> 11:59.700
I wonder what the elvish people 
will think if their princess

11:59.700 --> 12:02.150
dies in human territory?

12:06.130 --> 12:08.660
You just said our magic wasn't working!

12:13.540 --> 12:14.940
You kept trying too, Vio!

12:33.190 --> 12:34.190
Vio?!

12:41.330 --> 12:42.280
Oh, no.

12:45.700 --> 12:46.820
Run!

12:59.710 --> 13:00.750
You all right?

13:00.750 --> 13:03.700
Yeah. Getting saved by you, though...

13:03.700 --> 13:04.600
Seriously?

13:06.060 --> 13:07.470
Vio! Fey!

13:07.970 --> 13:09.020
We need to retreat.

13:09.020 --> 13:10.290
Seconded!

13:11.310 --> 13:12.470
I'm going to try again.

13:12.820 --> 13:14.430
This is no time to act headstrong.

13:14.430 --> 13:15.950
Let's just get out of here.

13:16.390 --> 13:17.480
Please!

13:17.980 --> 13:20.310
She must have come up with a plan.

13:20.310 --> 13:21.760
Oh, geez.

13:21.760 --> 13:24.490
Be ready to run the second you 
think you can't pull this off.

13:24.490 --> 13:26.120
Got it!

13:27.450 --> 13:28.470
Over here!

13:36.130 --> 13:38.140
Come on already! Chase after me!

13:42.130 --> 13:45.260
What in the world made me agree to this?!

13:46.620 --> 13:48.660
Physical labor isn't my forte!

13:55.510 --> 13:56.840
Vio, do it!

14:07.090 --> 14:09.410
Magic might not affect it...

14:10.460 --> 14:11.930
But how about this?

14:22.920 --> 14:24.860
I-It worked.

14:27.900 --> 14:32.090
Great work! I'm out of mana.

14:32.090 --> 14:34.430
And I'm out of stamina.

14:35.510 --> 14:37.220
Likewise...

14:57.300 --> 14:58.120
Tessia?!

14:58.430 --> 14:59.460
Stupid!

15:00.100 --> 15:02.100
Stupid's a little harsh.

15:02.100 --> 15:03.460
<i>What else was I supposed to do?</i>

15:04.130 --> 15:08.820
<i>It just seemed like the right 
thing to do at the time.</i>

15:08.820 --> 15:10.220
<i>Like what Arthur would've done.</i>

15:11.810 --> 15:13.220
<i>Arthur...</i>

15:16.260 --> 15:17.520
<i>Arthur.</i>

15:22.810 --> 15:23.990
<i>Arthur.</i>

15:40.860 --> 15:42.000
We need to retreat.

15:42.620 --> 15:43.670
Let's run.

15:48.260 --> 15:49.760
Tessia, no!

15:50.150 --> 15:53.510
Don't. You're out of mana, too.

15:53.970 --> 15:57.610
<i>I am out of mana. But Arthur 
taught me something.</i>

16:30.190 --> 16:31.010
What the...

16:31.340 --> 16:32.450
That's mana.

16:44.350 --> 16:45.470
Tessia!

16:45.470 --> 16:46.600
Run!

17:04.570 --> 17:06.580
She strengthened her body with mana?

17:07.180 --> 17:08.030
Seriously?

17:08.030 --> 17:09.380
Seriously hurts!

17:09.700 --> 17:11.020
Well, obviously!

17:11.020 --> 17:14.380
Don't suddenly start 
acting like an Augmenter!

17:17.830 --> 17:19.510
How unfortunate for you.

17:19.510 --> 17:22.640
Yes, she's more talented than I expected.

17:23.210 --> 17:26.900
I'll need to prepare a 
more powerful mana beast.

17:37.010 --> 17:39.660
Would it have killed him to thank us?

17:40.210 --> 17:42.300
Don't expect courtesy from humans.

17:42.300 --> 17:44.070
Still, though...

17:44.070 --> 17:45.850
What do you think, Tessia?

17:48.990 --> 17:52.120
See? The people who 
understand, understand.

17:53.430 --> 17:54.930
Miss Elf!

17:54.930 --> 17:56.060
Thank you!

17:57.470 --> 17:58.980
Is that where you live?

17:59.300 --> 18:00.100
Yeah.

18:00.100 --> 18:01.680
It's a nice house.

18:01.990 --> 18:04.530
Someone else used to live there.

18:04.530 --> 18:07.000
But they moved far away.

18:07.000 --> 18:09.500
They were supposed to be really strong.

18:11.480 --> 18:13.720
I know someone really strong, too.

18:13.720 --> 18:14.600
Really?

18:14.600 --> 18:16.190
What're they like?

18:17.080 --> 18:18.700
He's my goal.

18:28.510 --> 18:31.810
Good grief. She likes to cut it close.

18:32.660 --> 18:34.840
<i>How is she doing?</i>

18:35.080 --> 18:37.130
She took care of things safely.

18:37.130 --> 18:41.510
<i>I see. I should expect nothing 
less from your granddaughter.</i>

18:41.510 --> 18:45.850
As much as I'd like to take credit, 
she's been blessed with wonderful friends.

18:45.850 --> 18:47.100
<i>What friends?</i>

18:47.100 --> 18:49.600
Someone you know very well.

18:49.600 --> 18:51.840
<i>Oh, him...</i>

18:51.840 --> 18:55.110
Their brief time together will 
be enough to change the world.

18:56.710 --> 18:59.050
We'll make it so.

19:03.350 --> 19:05.620
Don't you agree, Cynthia?

19:08.350 --> 19:10.150
Yes, Virion.

19:18.060 --> 19:21.680
Fey and I are heading back to 
Xyrus. What about you, Vio?

19:21.680 --> 19:23.230
Going back to Elenoir?

19:23.230 --> 19:25.160
I dunno.

19:25.690 --> 19:28.500
If you are, using the gate 
at Xyrus will be faster.

19:28.500 --> 19:29.910
To Xyrus, then.

19:30.230 --> 19:32.900
It'll be nice to see Arthur again, too.

19:33.390 --> 19:35.900
Yeah. Wait, what?

19:36.190 --> 19:37.820
To Xyrus?

19:37.820 --> 19:39.450
After that!

19:39.450 --> 19:41.880
It'll be nice to see Arthur again?

19:41.880 --> 19:45.480
How?! How do you know about Arthur, Vio?!

19:45.480 --> 19:48.290
How couldn't I? I went to Xyrus with him.

19:48.290 --> 19:49.660
Oh, right!

19:50.090 --> 19:52.360
We've actually seen him pretty regularly.

19:52.360 --> 19:54.920
Allie is so beautiful!

19:55.230 --> 19:57.770
I remember they baked 
sweets for us once.

19:57.770 --> 19:59.870
That calls for some kind of thanks.

19:59.870 --> 20:02.060
And Eleanor is so cute!

20:02.060 --> 20:04.350
Mr. Reynolds is apparently an Augmenter.

20:04.350 --> 20:05.680
No...

20:05.680 --> 20:07.450
No fair!

20:07.450 --> 20:08.650
What's not fair?

20:08.650 --> 20:10.680
Have you not seen Arthur since he left?

20:10.920 --> 20:14.560
I mean, he never said 
where in Xyrus he went,

20:14.560 --> 20:16.170
and no one ever told me.

20:16.170 --> 20:17.900
You two are such cheaters!

20:19.140 --> 20:21.440
You're helpless, huh?

20:32.020 --> 20:34.460
This is Arthur's house.

20:35.070 --> 20:36.570
I finally get to see him.

20:37.640 --> 20:41.340
No, I need to think about how to do this.

20:41.340 --> 20:42.610
"Long time no see!"

20:42.610 --> 20:43.700
"I missed you!"

20:43.700 --> 20:44.660
"Here I am!"

20:44.660 --> 20:46.220
"Are you glad to see me?"

20:46.610 --> 20:47.970
Which should I go with?!

20:48.420 --> 20:51.470
No sense fretting over it. 
Let's see what happens!

20:51.470 --> 20:53.300
Can I help you with something?

20:53.300 --> 20:54.480
Yeah, can we?

20:55.740 --> 20:57.980
Excuse me!

20:58.260 --> 20:59.790
I wonder who that was.

20:59.790 --> 21:01.480
Bye bye!

21:03.990 --> 21:06.990
Where the heck are you, Arthur?!
